          "title": "Alabama Tried to Execute an Innocent Man for 30 Years",
          "description": "For thirty years, the state of Alabama prepared to execute Anthony Ray Hinton for two murders he did not commit. His conviction rested on discredited ballistics testimony and a defense that could not afford a qualified expert. This is how an innocent man survived death row — and how the Equal Justice Initiative and a unanimous U.S. Supreme Court (Hinton v. Alabama, 2014) finally set him free.\n\nPrime Documentary tells rigorously researched stories about justice and the law. This film includes AI-generated imagery used for illustration only; it is not authentic archival footage and depicts no real, identifiable individuals. Sources: the U.S. Supreme Court opinion in Hinton v. Alabama (2014), the Equal Justice Initiative, court records, and public reporting.\n\nIf this changed how you see the justice system, subscribe.",
